{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"explicit and implicit recommendation feedback explicit and implicit recommendation feedback","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","fileName":"Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-10-04 14:56\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Recommender System Evolution]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recommender System Evolution","Streaming Recommender System","recommendationengines.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"explicit and implicit recommendation feedback explicit and implicit recommendation feedback","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","fileName":"Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback","heading":"Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Explicit recommendation feedback is a deliberate statement such as a rating, review, like, or ranked preference. Implicit feedback is inferred from behavior such as a click, purchase, skip, replay, dwell time, or completion. Both describe user-item interaction, but they differ in effort, ambiguity, and scale.\n\nExplicit signals are easier to interpret but costly enough that users provide relatively few of them. Implicit signals arrive continuously and make a [[Streaming Recommender System]] responsive, yet the same action can have several explanations: a long view may indicate interest, distraction, or an unattended device. A reliable system evaluates behavioral evidence in context instead of treating every recorded action as an equally strong preference.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recommender System Evolution","Streaming Recommender System","recommendationengines.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"explicit and implicit recommendation feedback explicit and implicit recommendation feedback","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","fileName":"Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Explicit and Implicit Recommendation Feedback","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[recommendationengines.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recommender System Evolution","Streaming Recommender System","recommendationengines.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}